grt: global_route -unguided_only routes only the nets without guides

global_route -unguided_only keeps the global route guides of every net
that has them, as they are in the database, with the edge resources they
use, and routes only the nets that have none, around them. A net whose
guides do not cover its pins is routed too (GRT-0304). The guides of the
nets it routed are written; the others are left as they were read.

A top level whose blocks were dissolved into it after their own global
route (patch 0157) keeps every block's routes and routes only what it
built itself, its clock tree, instead of routing the whole design again:
stock grt restores guides only when every net has them (haveDbGuides)
and otherwise reroutes everything.

FastRoute only; with -use_cugr it stops (GRT-0338). GRT-0339 reports how
many nets kept their guides and how many were routed.

Test: unguided_only (gcd, five nets' guides cleared and routed again,
every other net's guides unchanged; a second run reroutes nothing).

Carried by bazel-orfs for //tools/carve; not upstreamed. Retires on a
//:bump onto an OpenROAD that carries it.
